  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#elements-2\r\n\r\n> There are six different kinds of elements:​ **void elements**, **the template element**, **raw text elements**, **escapable raw text elements**, **foreign elements**, and **normal elements**.\r\n> \r\n> ### Void elements\r\n> area, base, br, col, embed, hr, img, input, link, meta, param, source, track, wbr\r\n> ### The template element\r\n> template\r\n> ### Raw text elements\r\n> script, style\r\n> ### escapable raw text elements\r\n> textarea, title\r\n> ### Foreign elements\r\n> Elements from the MathML namespace and the SVG namespace.\r\n> ### Normal elements\r\n> All other allowed HTML elements are normal elements.\r\n\r\nCan you explain why there are no **custom elements** in this list? To which group does **custom elements** belong? Or do **custom elements** have their own group? Please clarify this point.",
